mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Instant Mechanic — Live Vehicle Service Operations Dashboard (Backend API)\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Purpose\n"
    # "\n"
    # "This canister is the backend for the Instant Mechanic live vehicle service\n"
    # "operations dashboard. It stores customers, mechanics, bookings, and service\n"
    # "categories, exposes aggregate dashboard and analytics statistics, lets an\n"
    # "operator advance a booking through its lifecycle, and seeds realistic demo\n"
    # "data plus a background simulator so the dashboard stays alive. It also\n"
    # "exposes its structured data through OQL so the Caffeine Data Intelligence\n"
    # "agent can answer natural-language questions over the stored tables.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Authentication\n"
    # "\n"
    # "All access is gated by Internet Identity sign-in through the app's frontend.\n"
    # "Anonymous callers are treated as guests. The first signed-in caller to\n"
    # "register becomes the **admin**; every subsequent registered caller becomes a\n"
    # "regular **user**. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the\n"
    # "app's own frontend, which calls `_initialize_access_control` (or the\n"
    # "`_internet_identity_sign_in_finish` flow) once per new principal.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n"
    # "`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding\n"
    # "the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\n"
    # "principal against that origin (for example\n"
    # "`icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\n"
    # "user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Authorization\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `assignCallerUserRole(user, role)` — **admin only**. Traps with\n"
    # "  `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles` when the caller is not\n"
    # "  an admin.\n"
    # "- `getCallerUserRole()` — returns the caller's role. Anonymous callers get\n"
    # "  `#guest`. A signed-in but unregistered caller traps with\n"
    # "  `User is not registered`.\n"
    # "- `isCallerAdmin()` — returns whether the caller is an admin.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "The dashboard data endpoints (`getDashboardStats`, `listBookings`,\n"
    # "`getBooking`, `updateBookingStatus`, `listMechanics`, `getMechanic`,\n"
    # "`listCustomers`, `getCustomer`, `listServiceCategories`, the analytics\n"
    # "endpoints, `seedDemoData`, and `simulatorTick`) do not enforce a role check in\n"
    # "the source; they are callable by any caller, including anonymous ones. The\n"
    # "OQL `schema` and `execute` endpoints are controller-only per entity (see\n"
    # "below).\n"
    # "\n"
    # "A caller can be unregistered even when the app already knows it: a\n"
    # "principal that never signed in through the app's own frontend is unregistered,\n"
    # "and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different\n"
    # "principal than the one the frontend registered.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Public Methods\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Dashboard\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `getDashboardStats() : DashboardStats` — aggregate stats: total bookings,\n"
    # "  today's bookings, completed / pending / cancelled counts, total revenue,\n"
    # "  active mechanics, and new customers in the last 30 days.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Bookings\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `listBookings(filter : BookingFilter) : BookingPage` — paginated, filterable\n"
    # "  (status, customer id, mechanic id, service category, date range, free-text\n"
    # "  search), sortable, with `page` / `limit` and a `total` count. Free-text\n"
    # "  search matches the customer's name (case-insensitive), vehicle make/model,\n"
    # "  service category, service description, and booking id.\n"
    # "- `getBooking(id : Nat) : ?Booking` — full booking detail, or `null` if the id\n"
    # "  does not exist.\n"
    # "- `updateBookingStatus(id : Nat, status : BookingStatus) : ?Booking` — advance\n"
    # "  a booking to a new status. Returns `null` if the booking does not exist.\n"
    # "  Returns the **unchanged** booking (not an error) when the requested\n"
    # "  transition is invalid (see Lifecycle). On a valid transition it also updates\n"
    # "  the assigned mechanic's status and `current_booking_id`.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Mechanics\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `listMechanics(filter : MechanicFilter) : MechanicPage` — paginated list with\n"
    # "  status, jobs completed, and current booking.\n"
    # "- `getMechanic(id : Nat) : ?Mechanic` — mechanic detail, or `null` if absent.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Customers\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `listCustomers(filter : CustomerFilter) : CustomerPage` — paginated list with\n"
    # "  free-text search.\n"
    # "- `getCustomer(id : Nat) : ?Customer` — customer detail, or `null` if absent.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Service Categories\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `listServiceCategories() : [ServiceCategory]` — all service categories.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Analytics\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `getBookingsOverTime(days : Nat) : [AnalyticsPoint]` — booking counts per\n"
    # "  period over the last `days`.\n"
    # "- `getRevenueOverTime(days : Nat) : [AnalyticsPoint]` — revenue per period over\n"
    # "  the last `days`.\n"
    # "- `getStatusBreakdown() : [StatusBreakdown]` — booking counts by status.\n"
    # "- `getCategoryBreakdown() : [CategoryBreakdown]` — booking counts by service\n"
    # "  category.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Simulation\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `seedDemoData() : ()` — seeds realistic demo data (customers, mechanics,\n"
    # "  bookings, service categories) if the bookings store is empty. Idempotent:\n"
    # "  it returns immediately when bookings already exist.\n"
    # "- `simulatorTick() : ()` — advances a few in-flight bookings through their\n"
    # "  lifecycle so the dashboard updates live without a real user acting.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### Authorization\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `assignCallerUserRole(user : Principal, role : UserRole) : ()` — admin-only\n"
    # "  role assignment.\n"
    # "- `getCallerUserRole() : UserRole` — the caller's role.\n"
    # "- `isCallerAdmin() : Bool` — whether the caller is an admin.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "### OQL\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `schema() : Text` — the OQL schema (JSON) describing the queryable entities.\n"
    # "- `execute(qJson : Text) : Executor.Result` — run an OQL query against the\n"
    # "  exposed entities.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Units and Encodings\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- **Amounts** are integers in the **smallest currency unit (cents)**, not\n"
    # "  dollars. Divide by 100 for display.\n"
    # "- **Timestamps** (`created_at`, `scheduled_at`, `updated_at`,\n"
    # "  `lastSimulatorTick`) are nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Int`).\n"
    # "- **Identifiers** (`id`, `customer_id`, `mechanic_id`) are `Nat`.\n"
    # "- **Optional fields**: `mechanic_id` and `current_booking_id` are `?Nat`;\n"
    # "  `null` means not assigned. In the OQL projection these are flattened to\n"
    # "  `0` when absent.\n"
    # "- **Statuses** are variants. Booking status: `#pending`, `#assigned`,\n"
    # "  `#on_the_way`, `#in_progress`, `#completed`, `#cancelled`. Mechanic status:\n"
    # "  `#available`, `#busy`, `#offline`. In OQL they are projected as their tag\n"
    # "  text (e.g. `on_the_way`).\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Lifecycle and Polling\n"
    # "\n"
    # "A booking progresses `pending → assigned → on_the_way → in_progress →\n"
    # "completed`, and may be cancelled from `pending`, `assigned`, `on_the_way`, or\n"
    # "`in_progress`. `completed` and `cancelled` are terminal. `updateBookingStatus`\n"
    # "rejects invalid transitions by returning the booking unchanged.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "The frontend polls the dashboard, bookings, mechanics, and analytics endpoints\n"
    # "roughly every **5 seconds** for live updates. `simulatorTick` (called by the\n"
    # "backend or an operator) advances in-flight bookings so statuses change between\n"
    # "polls. Polling is safe: all read endpoints are queries and have no side\n"
    # "effects.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Mutation Retry Safety\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- `updateBookingStatus` is safe to retry: an invalid transition is a no-op\n"
    # "  (returns the unchanged booking), and a valid transition is idempotent for\n"
    # "  the target status.\n"
    # "- `seedDemoData` is idempotent — it only seeds when the bookings store is\n"
    # "  empty, so re-calling it never duplicates data.\n"
    # "- `assignCallerUserRole` is idempotent — assigning the same role again is a\n"
    # "  no-op.\n"
    # "\n"
    # "## Errors and Gotchas\n"
    # "\n"
    # "- Authorization failures trap (reject the call) rather than returning an error\n"
    # "  value. `assignCallerUserRole` traps for non-admins; `getCallerUserRole`\n"
    # "  traps for signed-in but unregistered callers.\n"
    # "- `updateBookingStatus` returns `null` for a missing booking and the unchanged\n"
    # "  booking for an invalid transition — it does not raise an error for either.\n"
    # "- OQL entities are **controller-only**: only the platform controller (the\n"
    # "  Data Intelligence agent) can read them via `schema` / `execute`; end users\n"
    # "  cannot query them directly. The dashboard data endpoints above are the\n"
    # "  user-facing read path.\n"
    # "- Amounts are in cents and timestamps in nanoseconds — convert before display.\n"
  };
};
